@startsalt
' Screen: Dataset Import Wizard
' User Stories:
'   - US-414: As a developer, I can import entries from CSV, JSON, JSONL, or HuggingFace
'   - US-415: As a developer, I can map source columns to dataset fields
'   - US-416: As a developer, I can preview and validate entries before committing the import

{
  <b>Import Entries — Customer Support QA</b>                           [✕]
  ==
  {
    ● <b>Step 1: Source</b> | ─── | ○ Step 2: Column Mapping | ─── | ○ Step 3: Preview & Import
  }
  ==
  {
    <b>Step 1: Choose Source</b>
    --
    {
      (X) <b>CSV</b>  | ( ) <b>JSON</b>  | ( ) <b>JSONL</b>  | ( ) <b>HuggingFace Dataset</b>
    }
    --
    {
      <b>File Upload</b>
      {+
        "                                                                    "
        "         📂  Drag & drop CSV file here, or click to browse         "
        "              Accepted: .csv · Max size: 50 MB                     "
        "                                                                    "
      }
      [Browse File...]
    }
    ==
    <b>— OR — HuggingFace Dataset</b>
    --
    {
      <b>Dataset ID</b>
      "                                            "
      <i>e.g. rajpurkar/squad · tatsu-lab/alpaca</i>
    }
    {
      <b>Split</b>           | <b>Subset (optional)</b>
      ^train             ^ | "                      "
    }
    ==
    {
      [Cancel] | [Next: Map Columns →]
    }
  }
}
@endsalt
